    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (50 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `householdId` is now **deterministic** \u2014 the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` \u2014 so owners sharing lastName and postcode belong to the same household automatically.\n\n**`HouseholdId.java`** \u2014 added `compute(lastName, postcode)`: SHA-256 \u2192 first 12 hex chars, over the normalized lastName (trim/collapse-whitespace/lowercase) and postcode. Returns `null` when there's no postcode (a household of one).\n\n**`DeriveHouseholdId.java`** \u2014 reduced to computing and publishing the id. It no longer scans/backfills existing owners or gates on `sharesHousehold`; the id is derived the same way for every owner, so members compute the identical value independently.\n\n**`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 now enforces two 409 rules against stored owners:\n- *Identity duplicate*: exact `telephone|email|householdId` match \u2014 always rejects (even with `sharesHousehold`), which keeps Cp03/Cp25/Cp28 collisions intact.\n- *Household duplicate*: same computed `householdId` \u2014 rejects **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold`, which admits it as a declared member.\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 stamps the computed id onto every owner (with a postcode), not just opted-in ones. `AssignHouseholdSize` already keyed off `owner.householdId`, so household-size counting now uses the computed value with no change.\n\n**`DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 added a same-household guard: an existing owner in the same household is never a soft match, so a declared member is created and **not** flagged `possibleDuplicate` (Cp35).\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions for `householdId`/`sharesHousehold` and the affected Javadoc to match the new behaviour.\n\nThe key behavioural shift, as specified: `sharesHousehold` no longer *creates* the household link (the hash does) \u2014 it only *bypasses the duplicate block*.",
